    "title_en": "Axionic Casimir Torque",
    "abstract_en": "In the canonical Casimir effect, the quantum vacuum is isotropic, and the minimization of vacuum energy drives only a linear attractive force between the plates. However, the introduction of an axion gradient breaks this rotational symmetry. It can be demonstrated that these asymmetric zero-point fluctuations exert a macroscopic mechanical twist on the plates proportional to $\\vec{b}^2 \\sin (2\\vartheta)$ where $\\vec{b}$ is the spatial axion gradient and $\\vartheta$ is the angle between the axion gradient and the normal to the plates.",
